# IT routes: no gradient pill buttons

The teal-to-navy gradient pill (the Upload Contract / Upload License / Audit / Schedule / Report buttons in the top bar) is **not used inside the IT area**.

## Scope

- Every route under `/dashboard/it/**` (`src/app/(root)/dashboard/it/**`) and its components in `src/components/it/**`.
- The IT staff ticket surfaces: the `/tickets` queue and the `/tickets/[ticketId]` detail page and sheet (`src/components/tickets/detail/**`, `TicketDetail.tsx`, `TicketQueue.tsx`, `TicketsListWithSearch.tsx`).
- Not in scope: the company-wide ticket intake flow (`/tickets/new`, the Report issue FAB, the recorder) and the dark agent workspace's own palette.

## Forbidden in scope

- The `btn-primary` class, and its twins `primary-btn`, `shad-active`, `shad-submit-btn` (they all draw the same gradient pill).
- Hand-written copies of that look (`bg-[linear-gradient(90deg,#00c1cb,...)]`, `from-[#00c1cb] to-[#162768]` on a button).

## Use instead

```tsx
// Main action: solid brand blue
<Button variant="brand">Save</Button>
<Button asChild variant="brand"><Link href="...">Open</Link></Button>

// Secondary action: neutral outline
<Button variant="outline">Refresh</Button>

// Dismiss / cancel: ghost, never bordered
<Button variant="ghost">Cancel</Button>
```

`variant="brand"` lives in `src/components/ui/button.tsx`. Do not pass `px-3 sm:px-4`, a pill radius or a height override just to resize it; use the default size.

## When touching an IT file

Search the file for `btn-primary`, `primary-btn`, `shad-active`, `shad-submit-btn` and `00c1cb`. Swap every hit before finishing.
